On Friday 25 September 2009 17:14:50 Ivo Doko wrote:
> So I guessed right, I meant to say:
>
> le jvinu be vi ragve fe do
>
> Am I right in thinking that it means "The view from here is over there
> for you"? Perhaps "for you" was not the best choice of words here but
> I hope you see what I mean.

That is grammatical, but it's not a complete sentence. It's two sumti, "le 
jvinu be vi ragve" and "fe do", with no selbri. "le jvinu be vi ragve" is 
like "le vi jvinu ragve", except that "vi" modifies only "jvinu" (I'm not 
sure, I don't think I've seen such a construction). So the sentence 
means "The thing on the other side, having something to do with the here view 
— you (relation unspecified)".

Pierre


